low the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 36% clears the cost of capital of 9.2% by 27pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.98).","It converts 16% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.48x.","ROE of 27% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.4% of revenue on R&D and 2.8% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $2.7B (2% of market cap).","Goodwill makes up 36% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.0% over 3 years, 8.0% over 5 years and 7.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 13% of profits supports about 4.8% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 6.7% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.04, a backlog worth 50% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 8%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.3x, 1.0% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.0%), and institutions hold 85%.","Insider trading is two-way: 3 purchases and 10 sales over the past year, net $1.5M sold.","It returns 7.5% a year to shareholders (4.9% in buybacks and 2.6% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.7% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 20 consecutive years, raising it 9.4% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 814,000 employees, each generates about $91K of revenue, 0.2x the Technology median, and productivity has risen 7.6% a year.","That works out to $14K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $6.8M (74x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST",